{"seq":1,"at":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","register":"gapTypes","key":"Kinetic_Gap","label_en":"Kinetic gap","meaning_en":"A rule lacks the rate, affinity, or time constants (kcat·Km, Kd, half-life) needed to decide competition, duration, or termination.","xref":null,"since":"2026-10-16","prev":"97653dcef5a903d3491fcf66801ac3a4f08acbb4b4066e3b5ebf2ff4306e0285","root":"e3ca7ff0ce6be8e6007a4143ce2c6274db0f4652103792027b0b99624a0802e4"}
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","register":"gapTypes","key":"Concentration_Gap","label_en":"Concentration gap","meaning_en":"Molar concentration, molecules per cell, compartment volume, or mass balance is absent, so starting amounts rest on defaults or infinite pools.","xref":null,"since":"2026-10-16","prev":"e3ca7ff0ce6be8e6007a4143ce2c6274db0f4652103792027b0b99624a0802e4","root":"6ddcce0e0222b50448612b5cc616b4a48a30b47355134dc52a005457cec70974"}
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","register":"gapTypes","key":"Structural_Gap","label_en":"Structural gap","meaning_en":"3D coordinates, residue numbering, stoichiometry, or membrane topology is unknown or borrowed from another molecule.","xref":null,"since":"2026-10-16","prev":"6ddcce0e0222b50448612b5cc616b4a48a30b47355134dc52a005457cec70974","root":"3dc1f08b0e8fedaa8811f5c0dccabf1cc1a0b00785ccbfacb34dfddf74dc549d"}
{"seq":4,"at":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","register":"gapTypes","key":"Resource_Gap","label_en":"Resource (reservoir) gap","meaning_en":"No regeneration or supply path, or its rate, so a reservoir depletes and the pathway stalls; a post-mortem named it limiting. Closes when a supply rule's rate and starting amount arrive.","xref":null,"since":"2026-10-16","prev":"3dc1f08b0e8fedaa8811f5c0dccabf1cc1a0b00785ccbfacb34dfddf74dc549d","root":"63782d1def2dc6ddd3d18b49039e51e9a539840c445c5a6d85a66cef576818d3"}
{"seq":5,"at":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","register":"gapTypes","key":"Regulatory_Gap","label_en":"Regulatory-link gap","meaning_en":"Mediating steps of signal-to-metabolism or metabolism-to-gene regulation (receptor, STAT, mTORC1, chromatin) are lumped into one modulation rule, or its constants (K·n·fmax) are unknown.","xref":null,"since":"2026-10-16","prev":"63782d1def2dc6ddd3d18b49039e51e9a539840c445c5a6d85a66cef576818d3","root":"053da05ea9150be864a0475387213b245db8b2b68e351e051ec9b6108e1e3fdb"}
{"seq":6,"at":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","register":"gapTypes","key":"Observation_Gap","label_en":"Observation gap","meaning_en":"The error bars of available observations cannot separate competing hypotheses, or no observation exists to judge against.","xref":null,"since":"2026-10-16","prev":"053da05ea9150be864a0475387213b245db8b2b68e351e051ec9b6108e1e3fdb","root":"ebcd5db21434dd007e8dbe45249e0433da6a6b2585a561ccd08f93e7b5c048a9"}
